{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma (≈ 698.045 cents). Four fifths — E→B, B→F♯, A♭→E♭, E♭→B♭ — are each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma, equal to the equal-temperament fifth","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"2^(7\/12) ≈ 700.000 cents. The remaining four fifths are pure. The circle closes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly: 4×(1\/6) + 4×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Neidhardt relabeled this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specification “Small City” in his 1732 revision.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/neidhardti"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Neidhardt I (“Village”; Johann Georg Neidhardt, 1724)."}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE10neidhardtIAEvpZ::SYNTHESIZED::s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"neidhardtI"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"title":"neidhardtI"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/neidhardtI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types."}],"title":"IvorTuning","role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths.","type":"text"}],"title":"WellTemperament","role":"symbol",